{"type":"visualization","id":"agrishock-real-low-explanation","attributes":{"title":"Why the signal is LOW","visState":"{\"title\":\"Why the signal is LOW\",\"type\":\"markdown\",\"params\":{\"markdown\":\"## LOW is a deliberate conservative result\\n\\n- The observed movement is an **increase**, not a price decline. The potential distress-sale price-decline component is therefore **0**.\\n- +61.7% deviation and +6.37 robust z-score mean the price was unusual relative to the fixed baseline; they do **not** prove distress or causality.\\n- 144 ha is observed inundation, not a normalized severity score, so the severity contribution is **0**.\\n- No authoritative unaffected control market was captured; control comparison is **unavailable**.\\n- Temporal proximity contributes evidence.\\n\\nThe resulting 9.29 strength is a LOW market-shock signal, not a pipeline failure.\"},\"aggs\":[]}","uiStateJSON":"{}","kibanaSavedObjectMeta":{"searchSourceJSON":"{\"query\":{\"language\":\"kuery\",\"query\":\"fixture_kind: replayed_historical AND signal_id: 70ad06f7c3b849dd56b870c77f9dff20d187c802ec2d6c0eea7374f92b9e6c79\"},\"filter\":[]}"}},"references":[]}
